    "result_text": "The test passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change lets a project's invoices be sorted by due date. Since the database (`due_date` column, Flyway V6) and server (`InvoicesGet` returning `dueDate`) already store and surface the due date, this was an additive front-end change following the app's slot/URL-key conventions:\n\n- **`slots/defs/invoicesToolbar.ts`** (new) \u2014 declares an `invoices.toolbar` region above a project's invoices list, with `{ projectId }` context.\n- **`features/invoices/sort.slot.tsx`** (new) \u2014 a self-contained \"Sort by due date\" control (`data-testid=\"invoice-sort-due\"`) that fills the toolbar and owns the `invoiceSort` URL search-param key.\n- **`features/invoices/queries.ts`** \u2014 exported the shared `INVOICE_SORT_PARAM` key.\n- **`features/invoices/InvoicesTable.tsx`** \u2014 renders `<InvoicesToolbar.Slot>` and reads the same `invoiceSort` key to order its rows; due dates are ISO strings so a string compare is chronological (ascending).\n\nNo component passes callbacks or imports another feature \u2014 the sort control and the list coordinate purely through the shared URL key (CLAUDE.md rules 3\u20134). No DB migration or server change was needed since the due-date data already flows through.",
